{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "F14RaggedIndexSetIgnoresItsMemberFactor",
    "description": "FINDING F14, CONTROL \u2014 expected to PASS, and a control rather than a repro because the defect it recorded was resolved by settling the SPELLING, not by changing an evaluator.\n\nWHAT F14 CLAIMED, AND WHY IT WAS WRONG. This document used to assert that a `ragged` index set ignores its member factor: it declared `parentMember` as a flat `[1,2,3,4,5,6]`, ranged over the ragged axis, and read `index(flatValue, j)` \u2014 then reported 30 where 50 was wanted. The probe that seemed decisive was that REVERSING `parentMember` changed nothing. It changed nothing because the body never mentioned `parentMember` at all.\n\nWHAT THE FORMAT ACTUALLY SAYS, since EarthSciAST PR #352 made it normative (esm-spec \u00a74.3.1). A ragged range binds the POSITION k in 1..offsets[i], never a member; `offsets` is a per-parent LENGTH; and `values` is a PADDED [parent, max length] array, not a flattened CSR one. A body that wants the member gathers it: `index(values, i, k)`. The one exception is value invention (`distinct`, a `skolem` key, rank/argmin/argmax), where the range does bind the member. Upstream pins this repository's old spelling as `tests/invalid/faq/ragged_values_not_gathered.esm` \u2014 a document that MUST be rejected \u2014 and the correct one as `tests/valid/faq/ragged_member_gather.esm`.\n\nSO THIS IS THE CORRECT SPELLING, and it is kept because the member factor being READ is worth a standing check: `parentMember` is the padded [[1,0,0],[2,3,0],[4,5,6]], the body gathers `index(flatValue, index(parentMember, i, j))`, and the three parents total 10, 50 and 150. Measured: reversing the member rows moves those to 60, 90, 60 \u2014 so the factor is read, which is the counter-probe the original finding never ran.\n\nWHAT IT COST THE PORT: nothing. `components/movesoutput_aggregation.esm` keeps the flat row relation with the parent as a key column, which needs no padding and no axis machinery. The ragged axis is available for the nr-logging-county shape (3/4/29 model years per SCC) if a later stage wants it.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "finding",
      "resolved",
      "index-sets",
      "ragged"
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "parent_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 3
    },
    "max_members": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 3
    },
    "flat_member_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 6
    },
    "members_of_parent": {
      "kind": "ragged",
      "of": [
        "parent_rows"
      ],
      "offsets": "parentMemberCount",
      "values": "parentMember"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "F14RaggedIndexSetIgnoresItsMemberFactor": {
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
      },
      "variables": {
        "parentMemberCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "parent_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "offsets: the per-parent member COUNT -- one, two, three. Not a cumulative prefix sum."
        },
        "parentMember": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "parent_rows",
            "max_members"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "values: the PADDED [parent, max length] member array. Row i holds parent i's members in positions 1..offsets[i]; the trailing zeros are padding and are never read."
        },
        "flatValue": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "flat_member_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "A payload over the member axis, distinct per member so a mis-enumeration cannot coincide with the right answer."
        },
        "perParentTotal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "parent_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The sum of each parent's OWN members' payloads."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "parentMemberCount",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": [
              1,
              2,
              3
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "parentMember",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": [
              [
                1,
                0,
                0
              ],
              [
                2,
                3,
                0
              ],
              [
                4,
                5,
                6
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "flatValue",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": [
              10,
              20,
              30,
              40,
              50,
              60
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "j binds the POSITION in 1..parentMemberCount[i]; index(parentMember, i, j) gathers the member.",
          "lhs": "perParentTotal",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "semiring": "sum_product",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "parent_rows"
              },
              "j": {
                "from": "members_of_parent",
                "of": [
                  "i"
                ]
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "flatValue",
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "parentMember",
                    "i",
                    "j"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "a_ragged_axis_enumerates_its_parents_members",
          "description": "Per esm-spec \u00a74.3.1: the range binds the position and the body gathers the member, so parent 1 holds member 1 (10), parent 2 members 2 and 3 (50), parent 3 members 4, 5 and 6 (150). The original spelling, index(flatValue, j), gave 10, 30, 60 and is now rejected by validate() with `ragged_values_not_gathered`.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "perParentTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 10.0,
              "coords": {
                "parent_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "perParentTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 50.0,
              "coords": {
                "parent_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "perParentTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 150.0,
              "coords": {
                "parent_rows": 3
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
